   "evidence": "mathlib/Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/Ray.lean:42-44 `def SameRay ... := v\u2081 = 0 \u2228 v\u2082 = 0 \u2228 \u2203 r\u2081 r\u2082 ...`; :112 `theorem exists_pos (h : SameRay R x y) (hx : x \u2260 0) (hy : y \u2260 0) : \u2203 r\u2081 r\u2082 : R, 0 < r\u2081 \u2227 0 < r\u2082 \u2227 r\u2081 \u2022 x = r\u2082 \u2022 y`. This lemma is stated in the `AddCommMonoid` part of the file, so it works with the weakened hypotheses (unlike `exists_pos_left` at :593).",
   "file": "TauCeti/LinearAlgebra/Ray.lean",
   "fix": "Use the Mathlib lemma instead: `obtain \u27e8r\u2081, r\u2082, hr\u2081, hr\u2082, h\u27e9 := h.exists_pos (fun h0 \u21a6 hy.ne' (by simp [h0])) (fun h0 \u21a6 hz.ne' (by simp [h0]))`, then keep the existing `rw [\u2190 Prod.inv_fst_smul_snd_smul hr\u2081.ne' y, \u2190 Prod.inv_fst_smul_snd_smul hr\u2082.ne' z, h]`.",
   "issue": "`obtain h | h | \u27e8r\u2081, r\u2082, hr\u2081, hr\u2082, h\u27e9 := h` splits `SameRay R y z` by unfolding the body of Mathlib's `def SameRay` (a three-way disjunction). The proof breaks if Mathlib changes that definition, and it re-derives the two zero cases by hand.",
   "line": 258
  }
